  "goodToKnow": "Das Strafrecht is criminal law, mainly set out in the Strafgesetzbuch (StGB) from 1871, much amended. The opposite field is das Zivilrecht (civil law, in the BGB). Strafrechtlich verfolgt werden means to be prosecuted; ein Strafverteidiger is a criminal defence lawyer, and der Staatsanwalt the prosecutor. Germany has no jury trials; professional judges sit with lay judges (Schöffen). It has no plural."
